; A TYPE-CHOICE whose arm is an anonymous array wrapping a plain-group reference (`[coords] / tstr`)
; is SUPPORTED: the member-position array-of-plain-group path promotes `coords` to an Array-rep
; Record struct (via `set_rep_if_plain_group`, mirroring the homogeneous-array sibling), so the arm
; has a storable representation and generation emits a proper enum with a `Coords` variant that
; round-trips. This fixture records `ok` (not PANIC): it pins that this shape stays storable, guarding
; against a regression back to the `Option::unwrap()` on `None` panic in intermediate/rust_type.rs (variant
; naming/representation lookup) that the missing plain-group promotion used to trigger. The `any`-arm
; sibling (`any / tstr`, tests/robustness/choice_any_arm.cddl) still panics with the SAME message and
; keeps the recombination sweep's KNOWN_PANIC_CLASSES entry alive. Surfaced by the recombination sweep
; (src/tests/recombination_tests.rs).
coords = (uint, uint)
a = [coords] / tstr
